      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report an exceptional case of acute myocardial infarction due to thrombosis of the left main coronary artery in a 39-year old male patient. After failure of recanalization by systemic fibrinolysis, percutaneous angioplasty under circulatory assistance was successfully performed pending a possible transplantation. The patient unfortunately died of haemodynamic disturbances 48 hours after the infarction."},
